option.VOLUME_FAST_SHADOWS=Fast volume shadows
option.VOLUME_FAST_SHADOWS.comment=1-2 texel PCF per froxel (much faster; the froxels are already blurred and accumulated over time).
option.GLINT_STRENGTH=Enchantment Shine
option.GLINT_STRENGTH.comment=How bright the moving shine on enchanted items is.
option.GLINT_GLOW=Enchantment Glow
option.GLINT_GLOW.comment=How much the enchantment shine glows around the item.
option.EMISSIVE_BLOOM=Emissive glow
option.EMISSIVE_BLOOM.comment=Extra bloom on mob eyes (spider, enderman, phantom), light blocks and glowing particles.
option.BLOCK_GLOW=Block glow
option.BLOCK_GLOW.comment=How much glowing blocks (glowstone, lanterns, the glowing parts of sculk and redstone) glow around them, on top of Emissive glow. 1 = the same share as mob eyes, 0 = none.
option.CLOUD_OPACITY=Cloud opacity
option.CLOUD_OPACITY.comment=Absorption of the light crossing the cloud layer (0 = only Java's 0.8 alpha, which let the sun and moon show through).
option.PBR_TABLE.comment=Estimated roughness and metalness per block, for playing without a PBR resource pack. Metal, gem, obsidian and ore blocks texel by texel, like the target look texture sets: only the bright parts (iron plates, the relief of obsidian, the mineral) are smooth and reflective. Lights and foliage keep their emission and subsurface.

option.CLOUD_SOLAR_RIM=Cloud Solar Rim
option.CLOUD_SOLAR_RIM.comment=Sun and moon transmission across cloud undersides and exposed edges, depending on viewing angle and optical thickness. Soft style requires cloud lighting.
value.CLOUD_SOLAR_RIM.0=OFF
value.CLOUD_SOLAR_RIM.1=ON
option.CLOUD_RIM_STRENGTH=Cloud Rim Strength

option.SUN_LIGHT_BLEED=Sun and Moon Bloom
option.SUN_LIGHT_BLEED.comment=Feeds visible discs into existing emissive bloom. Spreads over silhouettes, stronger for the sun and softer for the moon. Requires Bloom.
value.SUN_LIGHT_BLEED.0=OFF
value.SUN_LIGHT_BLEED.1=ON
option.SUN_GLOW_STRENGTH=Celestial Bloom Strength
option.CLOUD_RIM_STYLE=Cloud Rim Style
value.CLOUD_RIM_STYLE.0=Previous
value.CLOUD_RIM_STYLE.1=Soft transmission
option.TAA=Temporal anti-aliasing (TAA)
option.TAA.comment=Depth-validated temporal accumulation and detail recovery. Enabled by default. Native resolution; not an upscaler.
option.TAA_BLEND=Maximum history weight
option.TAA_SHARPNESS=TAA sharpness
option.TAA_SHARPNESS.comment=Bounded detail recovery outside the history feedback. Zero disables sharpening; high values may emphasize noise.

option.RENDER_SCALE=Internal resolution
option.RENDER_SCALE.comment=Experimental 85%: temporal reconstruction at native output. Requires TAA; uses 100% when TAA is off.
value.RENDER_SCALE.100=Native (100%)
value.RENDER_SCALE.85=Quality (85%, test)

option.BIOME_GRADING=Biome colour grading
option.BIOME_GRADING.comment=Colour temperature per biome family (cold snow, warm jungles and savannas...).
value.BIOME_GRADING.0=Off
value.BIOME_GRADING.1=All day
value.BIOME_GRADING.2=Sunrise/sunset only

option.SUN_HALO_STRENGTH=Sun halo strength
option.SUN_HALO_STRENGTH.comment=The sky's glow around the sun near sunrise and sunset. 1 = full strength.
option.TAA_ANTI_FLICKER=TAA anti-flicker
option.TAA_ANTI_FLICKER.comment=Edges between leaves and what is behind them, the far edge of water against the sky and other edges of still surfaces no longer blink every few frames (mostly at 85% resolution): their history is kept and bounded by the colours around, as in the target look. Moving areas are resolved as before.
